[4mDLB[24m(6)                           Games Manual                           [4mDLB[24m(6)

[1mNAME[0m
       dlb - NetHack data librarian

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
       [1mdlb [22m{ [1mxct [22m} [ [1mvfIC [22m] arguments...  [ [1mfiles...  [22m]

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
       [4mDlb[24m  is  a file archiving tool in the spirit (and tradition) of tar for
       NetHack version 3.1 and higher.  It is used  to  maintain  the  archive
       files  from which NetHack reads special level files and other read-only
       information.  Note that like tar the command and option specifiers  are
       specified  as  a  continuous  string  and are followed by any arguments
       required in the same order as the option specifiers.

       ^?ALLDOCS This facility is optional and may be excluded during  NetHack
       configuration.   ^:  ^?DLB This facility is optional but is included in
       this NetHack configuration.  ^:  This  facility  is  optional  and  was
       excluded from this NetHack configuration.  ^.  ^.

[1mCOMMANDS[0m
       The  [1mx  [22mcommand  causes [4mdlb[24m to extract the contents of the archive into
       the current directory.

       The [1mc [22mcommand causes [4mdlb[24m to create a new archive from files in the cur-
       rent directory.

       The [1mt [22mcommand lists the files in the archive.

[1mOPTIONS AND ARGUMENTS[0m
       [1mv               [22mverbose output

       [1mf [4m[22marchive[24m      specify the archive.  Default if f not specified is LIB-
       FILE (usually the nhdat file in the playground).

       [1mI [4m[22mlfile[24m        specify the file containing the list of files to put  in
       to  or  extract  from the archive if no files are listed on the command
       line.  Default for archive creation if no files are listed is  LIBLIST-
       FILE.

       [1mC  [4m[22mdir[24m           change  directory.  Changes directory before trying to
       read any files (including the archive and the lfile).

[1mEXAMPLES[0m
       Create the default archive from the default file list:
                   dlb c

       List the contents of the archive 'foo':
                   dlb tf foo

[1mAUTHOR[0m
       Kenneth Lorber

[1mSEE ALSO[0m
       nethack(6), tar(1)

[1mBUGS[0m
       Not a good tar emulation; - does not  mean  stdin  or  stdout.   Should
       include  an optional compression facility.  Not all read-only files for
       NetHack can be read out of an archive; examining the source is the only
       way to know which files can be.

